-- title:
--   Reduced quotient B/(varpi) gives B integrally closed in B[1/varpi]
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative ring and let $\varpi \in B$ be an element belonging to the monoid of non-zero-divisors of $B$, and assume that the quotient ring $B / (\varpi)$, where $(\varpi)$ is the ideal generated by the singleton $\{\varpi\}$, is reduced. Let $L$ be a commutative ring equipped with a $B$-algebra structure which realises $L$ as the localisation of $B$ away from $\varpi$, that is, the localisation at the multiplicative monoid of powers of $\varpi$. The conclusion is that $B$ is integrally closed in $L$: the structure map $B \to L$ is injective, and every element of $L$ that is integral over $B$ (a root of some monic polynomial with coefficients in $B$) lies in the image of $B \to L$. Informally, $B$ is integrally closed in $B[1/\varpi]$.
--
--   This is the standard 'reduced special fibre implies no new integral elements' lemma underlying Dedekind's criterion and descriptions of normalisations. It is used in the project to verify integral closedness of orders of the shape $\mathcal{O}[x]$ attached to a squarefree reduction, and in the analysis of tensor products with reduced fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsIntegrallyClosedIn_of_isReduced_quotient_span_singleton.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem IsIntegrallyClosedIn.of_isReduced_quotient_span_singleton
    {B : Type*} [CommRing B] (ϖ : B) (hϖ : ϖ ∈ nonZeroDivisors B)
    [IsReduced (B ⧸ Ideal.span {ϖ})]
    (L : Type*) [CommRing L] [Algebra B L] [IsLocalization.Away ϖ L] :
    IsIntegrallyClosedIn B L := by sorry
